  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 245 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThe GFS/ECMWF is showing an upper ridge building over the western \nCONUS Thursday into Friday which keeps northwest upper flow over \nMissouri and Illinois.  Showers and thunderstorm chances will \nincrease over the area beginning late Thursday night and continues \ninto Saturday with the NBM/LREF showing the highest chances (40-70%) \non Friday morning when the low level jet will be focused over the \narea. There will also be a upper trough that will move across \nMissouri and Illinois that both the determistic models and the LREF \nis showing timing differences which keeps PoPs in the forecast into \nSaturday.   This spread in timing will decrease in coming days as \nthe models come into the better agreement.  The LREF is showing \nPWATS around 2\" and WPC is highlighting most of the Missouri \ncounties in slight risk for excessive rainfall on Friday. The LREF \nthen shows the upper ridge shifting east and building over the \ncentral CONUS.  This keeps the area mainly dry from late weekend \nthrough the first part of next week.\n\nTemperatures on Friday will remain cool with clouds, the chance of \nrain, and the cool surface flow.  Highs will begin to warm back \nabove normal by Sunday as a warm front moves back through the area \nand 850mb temperatures climb back above 20C.",
